# The same proof with the verifier's first check omitted.
#
# Belenios verifies "A0 != 1" before anything else, and that check is
# load-bearing in a way the equations do not show.  The map is
# injective exactly when the encrypted value is non-zero: from the
# first equation v = -r*u, and substituting into the second leaves
# A0 = g^(m*u), so u is pinned only when m is non-zero -- and when m
# is zero, A0 is forced to 1.
#
# A verifier that dropped the check would be looking at this, where
# every target is the identity.  The all-zero witness satisfies it, so
# the proof demonstrates nothing at all.
secrets u v
claims  u v
eq  1   alpha  g
eq  1   beta   y
